\DOC LOCAL_SUB_P256K1_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_SUB_P256K1_TAC : int -> string list -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances a machine-state symbolic-execution goal across an inlined
modular-subtraction subroutine, replacing the current state variable by its
successor and adding a conditional specification of the computed result.

\DESCRIBE
{LOCAL_SUB_P256K1_TAC n [out; in1; in2]} takes an {int} (the same fixed value
in all observed traces) and a {string list} of three names identifying the
output variable and the two input variables of the subtraction step, in terms
of which the generated specification is phrased. The goal is an {eventually}
statement about a current state variable {s}; the tactic yields exactly one
subgoal in which {s} is replaced by a successor state {s'}, both in the
conclusion and in every assumption mentioning it. Concretely, each
state-dependent assumption — the program-counter reading, the code-loaded
assumption, register readings, memory-block readings, and the accumulated
{MAYCHANGE} relation from the initial state — is discharged and re-added for
{s'}, with an updated program-counter value, a possibly extended {MAYCHANGE}
list, and a new memory-block reading equating the output buffer with a fresh
variable {r} for the subtraction result. Purely mathematical assumptions are
kept unchanged, sometimes reordered. One further assumption is added: an
implication whose antecedents bound the two input values below the modulus and
whose conclusion equates {r} with the integer remainder of the difference of
the inputs modulo the modulus.
{
   A, state-dependent assumptions about s, mathematical assumptions ?- eventually ... s
   ================================================================================  LOCAL_SUB_P256K1_TAC n [out; in1; in2]
   state-dependent assumptions about s' (updated pc, extended MAYCHANGE, output buffer = r),
   mathematical assumptions,
   (in1 < modulus /\ in2 < modulus ==> r = (in1 - in2) rem modulus)
     ?- eventually ... s'
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this single kind of outcome occurs, always on goals
of this symbolic-execution form with a large assumption list.

\ENDDOC
